        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Railroad Labor Board\n- People: Calvin Coolidge\n- Laws: Railway Labor Act\n- Places: Vermont, Massachusetts\n- Roles: Republican lawyer, governor\n\nFacts:\n- Calvin Coolidge was a Republican lawyer from Vermont.\n- Calvin Coolidge advanced through Massachusetts state politics and eventually became governor of Massachusetts.\n- On May 20, 1926, President Calvin Coolidge signed a new Railway Labor Act into law.\n- The Railroad Labor Board was terminated on May 20, 1926, when President Calvin Coolidge signed the new Railway Labor Act into law.",
